<%# The wait screen for a Verto being generated in the background. This is the
    screen the creator actually watches for the 30-120s a build takes — the
    wizard's own overlay only shows for the moment before the redirect lands
    here — so it runs the full staged experience (shared/_generating_stage +
    generating_controller in autostart mode): rotating hero messages, brief
    pills, insight quote and step dots, not a static title.

    Difference from the overlay: this one is real. It reflects a build row, so
    a refresh, a closed laptop or a flaky connection all resume correctly —
    including the stage theatre, which picks up from the build's elapsed time
    instead of restarting. %>
<div class="fixed inset-0 z-50 flex flex-col overflow-hidden"
     style="background:#1C2034;"
     data-controller="verto-build generating"
     data-verto-build-url-value="<%= verto_build_path(@build, format: :json) %>"
     data-generating-autostart-value="true"
     data-generating-kind-value="<%= @build.kind %>"
     data-generating-theme-value="<%= @build.payload["theme"] %>"
     data-generating-age-value="<%= @build.payload["audience_age"] %>"
     data-generating-insight-value="<%= @build.payload["key_insight"] %>"
     data-generating-elapsed-value="<%= (Time.current - @build.created_at).round %>">

  <%= render layout: "shared/generating_stage" do %>
    <%# Only shown if polling itself breaks — the build keeps running on the
        server regardless, so the copy points at a reload rather than a retry. %>
    <div class="hidden" data-verto-build-target="stalled"
         style="font-family:'ABeeZee',sans-serif;font-size: var(--text-base);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5);text-align:center;max-width:520px;line-height:1.5;">
      Still working. This page will update on its own — you can also reload it,
      or come back to it later from your dashboard.
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
